6 + 4 + 2 = 12 gifts in total. She wants to make a bow for each gift. So she will make 12 bows. She has 144 inches of ribbon. To find out how much ribbon she can use for each bow, we need to divide the total amount of ribbon by the number of bows. So, 144 inches / 12 bows = 12 inches per bow.
Therefore, she can use 12 inches of ribbon for each gift bow.
