completions_8:
1. Calculate the number of slices Bill receives:
   \begin{itemize}
   \item Jenny gives \frac{1}{3} of the pizza to Bill.
   \item The total number of slices is 12.
   \item The number of slices Bill receives is \frac{1}{3} \times 12 = 4 \text{ slices}.
   \end{itemize}
Bill receives 4 slices.

2. Calculate the number of slices Mark receives:
   \begin{itemize}
   \item Jenny gives \frac{1}{4} of the pizza to Mark.
   \item The total number of slices is 12.
   \item The number of slices Mark receives is \frac{1}{4} \times 12 = 3 \text{ slices}.
   \end{itemize}
Mark receives 3 slices.

3. Calculate the total number of slices given away:
   \begin{itemize}
   \item Bill receives 4 slices.
   \item Mark receives 3 slices.
   \item Jenny eats 2 slices.
   \item The total number of slices given away and eaten is 4 + 3 + 2 = 9 \text{ slices}.
   \end{itemize}
Total slices given away and eaten is 9.

4. Calculate the number of slices remaining:
   \begin{itemize}
   \item The total number of slices is 12.
   \item The number of slices given away and eaten is 9.
   \item The number of slices remaining is 12 - 9 = 3 \text{ slices}.
   \end{itemize}
There are 3 slices remaining.

\boxed{3}
